nce the link function from decision_function() to predict_proba()\n3754 |         # is sometimes not precise enough (typically expit), we round to the\n3755 |         # 10th decimal to avoid numerical issues: we compare the rank\n3756 |         # with deterministic ties rather than get platform specific rank\n3757 |         # inversions in case of machine level differences.\n3758 |         a = estimator.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1].round(decimals=10)\n3759 |         b = estimator.decision_function(X_test).round(decimals=10)\n3760 | \n3761 |         rank_proba, rank_score = rankdata(a), rankdata(b)\n3762 |         try:\n3763 |             assert_array_almost_equal(rank_proba, rank_score)\n3764 |         except AssertionError:\n3765 |             # Sometimes, the rounding applied on the probabilities will have\n3766 |             # ties that are not present in the scores because it is\n3767 |             # numerically more precise. In this case, we relax the test by\n3768 |             # grouping the decision function scores based on the probability\n3769 |             # rank and check that the score is monotonically increasing.\n3770 |             grouped_y_score = np.array(\n3771 |                 [b[rank_proba == group].mean() for group in np.unique(rank_proba)]\n3772 |             )\n3773 |             sorted_idx = np.argsort(grouped_y_score)\n3774 |             assert_array_equal(sorted_idx, np.arange(len(sorted_idx)))\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"docstring consistency\", \"assert_consistent_docs docstring consistency\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `doc/api_reference.py:_get_submodule`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n21 | def _get_submodule(module_name, submodule_name):\n22 |     \"\"\"Get the submodule docstring and automatically add the hook.\n23 | \n24 |     `module_name` is e.g. `sklearn.feature_extraction`, and `submodule_name` is e.g.\n25 |     `image`, so we get the docstring and hook for `sklearn.feature_